{"case_id":"C012","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","configuration","input_semantics"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["ares__get_hostent","ares__readaddrinfo","fake_addrinfo","fake_hostent","ip_addr"],"reason":"H0 covers DNS reply parsing and ares_create_query with a fixed AAAA query, but it never exercises the changed IPv4 text-conversion paths. S1 routes host-file records, numeric names, and initialization/configuration addresses through ares_inet_pton, creating fuzz-worthy acceptance and rejection boundaries, including malformed dotted-decimal strings and 255.255.255.255.","evidence":["ares-test-fuzz.c invokes only ares_parse_a_reply, ares_parse_aaaa_reply, ares_parse_ptr_reply, ares_parse_ns_reply, ares_parse_srv_reply, ares_parse_mx_reply, ares_parse_txt_reply, ares_parse_soa_reply, and ares_parse_naptr_reply.","ares-test-fuzz-name.c sends arbitrary bytes only to ares_create_query(name, ns_c_in, ns_t_aaaa, ...); it does not invoke fake_addrinfo, fake_hostent, ares__get_hostent, ares__readaddrinfo, or ip_addr.","S1 replaces inet_addr with ares_inet_pton(AF_INET, ...) in ares__get_hostent and ares__readaddrinfo, which parse textual addresses from FILE input.","S1 changes numeric-name recognition in fake_addrinfo and fake_hostent from an INADDR_NONE comparison to the return value of ares_inet_pton.","S1 changes the initialization helper ip_addr to rely entirely on ares_inet_pton and removes its explicit 255.255.255.255 exception."],"recommended_action":"Add fuzz targets that drive numeric-host handling through the getaddrinfo/gethostbyname paths, feed structured host-file text to ares__get_hostent and ares__readaddrinfo, and exercise initialization address configuration reaching ip_addr. Include valid, malformed, truncated, embedded-NUL, boundary-octet, and 255.255.255.255 inputs."}
